{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-011-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/AdaptiveSamplingTests.cs","line":178,"method":"SmallSpeedNearFloor_NoFalsePositive","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.cs:75; raise the 0.1f speed reference floor to 1f -> red","what_it_asserts":"ShouldRecordPoint returns true for 0.05 to 0.06 m/s because the 0.1 m/s reference floor makes the ratio 10 percent.","why_weak":"The name promises no false positive but the assertion is Assert.True and the inline comment concedes it records. A reader scanning names concludes the floor suppresses near-zero jitter when it does not.","proposed_action":"Rename to SmallSpeedNearFloor_ReferenceFloorMakesRatioSignificant_Records, or add the genuine no-false-positive case (0.05 to 0.0501) asserting false.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-011-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/AdaptiveSamplingTests.cs","line":245,"method":"ZeroTimeDelta_NoRecord","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.cs:57; change elapsed >= maxInterval to elapsed <= maxInterval -> red","what_it_asserts":"ShouldRecordPoint returns false when currentUT equals lastRecordedUT.","why_weak":"Both velocities are identical, so no gate could fire whatever the elapsed handling is. Production has no zero-delta guard: with minInterval 0 the floor check 0 < 0 is false, so a velocity change at the same UT does record and writes a duplicate-UT sample. The name claims a guard that does not exist.","proposed_action":"Repeat the case with a 10 to 11 m/s change at zero and negative elapsed and assert the intended behaviour; add an explicit non-positive elapsed guard in ShouldRecordPoint if duplicate-UT samples are unwanted.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-011-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/AdaptiveSamplingTests.cs","line":366,"method":"MinInterval_HighSpeedAscent_NoLossVsLegacy","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.cs:61; change elapsed < minInterval to elapsed < minInterval * 5f -> red","what_it_asserts":"Commit count with a 0.2s floor is at least the legacy count minus 1 over a simulated 50 Hz ascent.","why_weak":"Purely relative with one commit of slack and no absolute pin. Both runs produce 2 commits today; a regression that silences the velocity gates entirely leaves 0 >= -1 green, and deleting the floor line makes the runs identical and green.","proposed_action":"Assert the absolute commit count of each run (Assert.Equal(2, commitsLegacy) and Assert.Equal(2, commitsWithFloor)) alongside the inequality.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recorder-events-011-04","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/AdaptiveSamplingTests.cs","line":257,"method":"BackwardTime_NoRecord","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.cs:57; change elapsed >= maxInterval to elapsed <= maxInterval -> red","what_it_asserts":"ShouldRecordPoint returns false when currentUT is one second before lastRecordedUT.","why_weak":"The two velocities are identical, so the false result survives deletion of every elapsed-related line; only an inverted max-interval comparison reds it. The negative-elapsed case is actually handled by the minInterval floor at TrajectoryMath.cs:61, which this data never reaches meaningfully.","proposed_action":"Use a velocity pair that would otherwise fire the speed gate (10 to 11 m/s) so the false result is attributable to the backward elapsed.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"TrajectoryMath","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/TrajectoryMath.cs","sut_line":42,"case_kind":"negative","proposed_name":"ShouldRecordPoint_NonPositiveElapsedWithVelocityChange_DoesNotRecord","sketch":"last=(10,0,0), current=(11,0,0); call with currentUT equal to lastRecordedUT and again with currentUT below it, minInterval 0; assert false for both.","guards":"A duplicate-UT or backward-UT trajectory sample being appended when the speed gate fires; today nothing blocks the zero-delta case and only the floor accidentally blocks the backward case.","risk":"recording"}
